ven do  it  and the pandemic was shutting new york  and la down and we there was a real  chance that we would have undeveloped  negative for the entire  shoot so it was just insanity i don't  recommend shooting on film during a  pandemic but  i had i honestly had not thought that  about  what you just said that the pandemic  would make it so you couldn't develop  the film couldn't develop  i know we were we had you know worst  case scenarios  all planned out fridges this what are we  gonna do if we have  you know canisters of undeveloped film  in the caribbean  what if there was a power outage you  know like you you we need a generator on  top of you know  a million things had to be thought about  i'm so i i can't believe your producers  let you shoot film  until luckily yeah luckily it's just my  money so it worked out i was  i was the insane insane person risking  it and  listen this this could have been a real  cautionary tale that you'd be talking  about going did you hear what happened  to  tonight when he tried to pay for his own  movie in the caribbean during the  pandemic and  the whole half his movie melted this is  actually  the other thing i wanted to address with  you i had heard that you had been paying  for your recent movies  yourself yeah i am curious um talk which  movies have you actually paid for  and at what point does like your wife  say to you no  you know here i i paid for the visit  split  glass and and old all four of those and  i pay for servant as well  and and and the reason that i do it is  to to do it at the smallest number where  i can be  um free and i can do something  provocative and different and unusual  and i'm not putting my partners at risk  i'm i'm taking the risk  and uh in most scenarios because we're  doing it at such a small price  we're gonna be okay you know no matter  what and so we can make the most  most interesting art i don't have to  think about it some equation of safety i  don't i don't have to think about that  